      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day). A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and there is no added benefit.\n\nThis may be a typo. Here are some common options:\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a standard anti-inflammatory dose.\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the absolute maximum, usually only for a short course.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours as needed**, for pain or fever.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you intended, or confirm that you really want 1600 mg four times daily. If you want that, I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first. I can add a note to the order if that helps."
      }
     ],
